---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  nav="wedding"
  title="Wedding Suits — Sam's Menswear · Vaughan"
  description="Wedding suits and tuxedos, measured personally by Sam. Groom, groomsmen, fathers — fitted from one tape."
>

  <!-- PAGE HERO -->
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div data-reveal>
        <div class="eyebrow-rule">House № 01 &middot; Wedding</div>
        <h1>The suit he <em>will be remembered in.</em></h1>
        <p class="lede">A wedding suit is the single most photographed garment of a man's life. Sam draws each one personally — lapel, cuff, button-stance and lining — from the groom's first measure to the groomsmen's last fitting.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- STORY + SKETCH SPLIT -->
  <section class="section tight">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split wide-left" data-reveal>
        <div>
          <h2 class="h-2" style="text-transform: uppercase;">A wedding party, <em style="font-style: italic; font-weight: 400; text-transform: none; color: var(--oxblood);">cut from one&nbsp;hand.</em></h2>
          <p class="body-prose" style="margin-top: 24px;">
            The groom is the lead, but never the only one drawn. Sam fits the father of the groom, the father of the bride, the brothers, the best man, and the ring-bearer — measuring all of them against the same notebook, so the wedding photographs read as one tailored line.
          </p>
          <p class="body-prose" style="margin-top: 18px;">
            Tuxedos in midnight wool with satin peak lapels. Three-piece suits in deep navy, charcoal, oxblood, or hunter green. Morning coats for the traditional. Cummerbunds, waistcoats, bow ties and braces, all from the house cloth.
          </p>
          <p style="margin-top: 32px;">
            <a href="/book" style="font-family: var(--serif); font-style: italic; letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-strong); padding-bottom: 2px;">Begin a wedding consultation&nbsp;&nbsp;&rarr;</a>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div style="aspect-ratio: 4 / 5; background: var(--paper-cream); border: 1px solid var(--rule); padding: 24px; position: relative; overflow: hidden;">
            <div class="crop-marks"></div>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 280 360" style="width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block;" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet">
              <g fill="none" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path d="M70 90 C 80 70, 120 60, 140 60 C 160 60, 200 70, 210 90"/>
                <path d="M126 92 C 110 130, 90 170, 76 200 C 70 215, 80 222, 100 225 C 122 230, 138 248, 140 270"/>
                <path d="M154 92 C 170 130, 190 170, 204 200 C 210 215, 200 222, 180 225 C 158 230, 142 248, 140 270"/>
                <path d="M70 90 C 56 140, 50 200, 56 270 C 60 310, 70 340, 84 348"/>
                <path d="M210 90 C 224 140, 230 200, 224 270 C 220 310, 210 340, 196 348"/>
                <path d="M84 348 L 196 348"/>
                <path d="M140 270 L 140 346"/>
                <circle cx="140" cy="270" r="3.5"/>
                <circle cx="140" cy="300" r="3.5"/>
                <circle cx="140" cy="330" r="3.5"/>
                <path d="M80 310 L 132 304 L 134 322 L 82 328 Z"/>
                <path d="M200 310 L 148 304 L 146 322 L 198 328 Z"/>
                <path d="M140 88 L 122 80 L 122 96 L 140 92 L 158 96 L 158 80 L 140 88 Z" fill="var(--oxblood)" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="1.2"/>
                <rect x="136" y="84" width="8" height="14" fill="var(--oxblood-deep)" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="1"/>
                <circle cx="100" cy="180" r="5" fill="var(--oxblood)" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="0.8"/>
                <circle cx="100" cy="180" r="2" fill="var(--gold)"/>
              </g>
              <g fill="rgba(28, 37, 64, 0.18)">
                <path d="M70 92 C 56 140, 50 200, 56 270 C 60 310, 70 340, 84 348 L 132 348 L 140 270 C 138 248, 122 230, 100 225 C 80 222, 70 215, 76 200 C 90 170, 110 130, 126 92 Z"/>
                <path d="M210 92 C 224 140, 230 200, 224 270 C 220 310, 210 340, 196 348 L 148 348 L 140 270 C 142 248, 158 230, 180 225 C 200 222, 210 215, 204 200 C 190 170, 170 130, 154 92 Z"/>
              </g>
              <g font-family="Cormorant Garamond" font-style="italic" font-size="10" fill="var(--ink-mute)" letter-spacing="2">
                <text x="34" y="80">peak lapel</text>
                <line x1="60" y1="80" x2="74" y2="100" stroke="var(--ink-mute)" stroke-width="0.6"/>
                <text x="218" y="200">midnight</text>
                <line x1="216" y1="200" x2="200" y2="220" stroke="var(--ink-mute)" stroke-width="0.6"/>
                <text x="38" y="220">boutonniere</text>
                <line x1="84" y1="220" x2="100" y2="190" stroke="var(--ink-mute)" stroke-width="0.6"/>
                <text x="142" y="56" text-anchor="middle">№ 01 · The Groom</text>
              </g>
            </svg>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FABRIC LIBRARY -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
        <div class="chapter-no">No. 02</div>
        <h2 class="h-1" style="text-transform: uppercase; max-width: 16ch;">The wedding <em>cloth library.</em></h2>
        <div class="right">House &amp; mill cloths</div>
      </div>

      <div class="swatch-rail" data-reveal>
        <div class="swatch swatch--navy swatch--dark"><div class="swatch__meta">Worsted · 280g</div><div class="swatch__name">Midnight Navy</div></div>
        <div class="swatch swatch--charcoal swatch--dark"><div class="swatch__meta">Italian super 130s</div><div class="swatch__name">Charcoal Chalk</div></div>
        <div class="swatch swatch--oxblood swatch--dark"><div class="swatch__meta">Mohair blend</div><div class="swatch__name">Oxblood Velvet</div></div>
        <div class="swatch swatch--herringbone swatch--dark"><div class="swatch__meta">English herringbone</div><div class="swatch__name">Hunter Green</div></div>
        <div class="swatch swatch--espresso swatch--dark"><div class="swatch__meta">Worsted flannel</div><div class="swatch__name">Tobacco Brown</div></div>
        <div class="swatch swatch--cream"><div class="swatch__meta">Linen / silk</div><div class="swatch__name">Ivory Dinner</div></div>
        <div class="swatch swatch--check swatch--dark"><div class="swatch__meta">Glen check</div><div class="swatch__name">Country Estate</div></div>
      </div>
      <p class="chapter-no" style="margin-top: 24px; text-align: center;">— Scroll for more —</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- LOOKBOOK -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
        <div class="chapter-no">No. 03</div>
        <h2 class="h-1" style="text-transform: uppercase; max-width: 18ch;">From the <em>wedding folio.</em></h2>
        <div class="right">Recent grooms</div>
      </div>
      <div class="lookbook" data-reveal>
        <div class="lb-tile lb-1"><div class="placeholder"><div class="corner">Folio · I</div><div class="label">Groom in three-piece midnight navy</div><div class="meta">King Edward Hotel · Toronto</div></div></div>
        <div class="lb-tile lb-2"><div class="placeholder"><div class="corner">Folio · II</div><div class="label">Boutonniere &amp; lapel</div><div class="meta">Wedding detail</div></div></div>
        <div class="lb-tile lb-3"><div class="placeholder"><div class="corner">Folio · III</div><div class="label">Best man &amp; brothers</div><div class="meta">Wedding party</div></div></div>
        <div class="lb-tile lb-4"><div class="placeholder"><div class="corner">Folio · IV</div><div class="label">Bow tie &amp; satin lapel</div><div class="meta">Black tie detail</div></div></div>
        <div class="lb-tile lb-5"><div class="placeholder"><div class="corner">Folio · V</div><div class="label">First look, navy three-piece</div><div class="meta">Outdoor ceremony</div></div></div>
        <div class="lb-tile lb-6"><div class="placeholder"><div class="corner">Folio · VI</div><div class="label">Cufflinks &amp; french cuff</div><div class="meta">Custom shirt detail</div></div></div>
        <div class="lb-tile lb-7"><div class="placeholder"><div class="corner">Folio · VII</div><div class="label">Father &amp; son, the morning of</div><div class="meta">Wedding preparation</div></div></div>
        <div class="lb-tile lb-8"><div class="placeholder"><div class="corner">Folio · VIII</div><div class="label">Pocket square &amp; trouser break</div><div class="meta">Final fitting</div></div></div>
        <div class="lb-tile lb-9"><div class="placeholder"><div class="corner">Folio · IX</div><div class="label">Tuxedo, single satin button</div><div class="meta">Black tie · 2025</div></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE PROMISE / DETAILS -->
  <section class="section"
           style="background: linear-gradient(180deg, transparent 0%, var(--paper-cream) 50%, transparent 100%);">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
        <div class="chapter-no">No. 04</div>
        <h2 class="h-1" style="text-transform: uppercase; max-width: 18ch;">What's <em>included.</em></h2>
        <div class="right">From measure to morning-of</div>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-grid cols-3" data-reveal-stagger>
        <div>
          <div class="feature-num">№ I</div>
          <h3 class="h-3">Personal consultation</h3>
          <p class="body-prose" style="margin-top: 12px;">A long, unhurried conversation about the wedding — the venue, the season, the colour story, the bride's gown, the photographs you want in twenty years.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="feature-num">№ II</div>
          <h3 class="h-3">Twenty-six measurements</h3>
          <p class="body-prose" style="margin-top: 12px;">Taken in person by Sam. Re-checked at each fitting. A pattern is drafted just for you — not adjusted from a template, not graded from a size.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="feature-num">№ III</div>
          <h3 class="h-3">Three fittings</h3>
          <p class="body-prose" style="margin-top: 12px;">Basted, intermediate, and final. The garment learns the shape of you across each one. Tiny corrections — drop of shoulder, sleeve pitch, trouser break — are made by hand.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="feature-num">№ IV</div>
          <h3 class="h-3">Groomsmen co‑ordinated</h3>
          <p class="body-prose" style="margin-top: 12px;">Up to ten groomsmen drawn from the same fabric run, with consistent lapel, button and pocket detail so the wedding line reads as one tailored party.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="feature-num">№ V</div>
          <h3 class="h-3">Pressed &amp; delivered</h3>
          <p class="body-prose" style="margin-top: 12px;">Pressed the morning of, boxed in tissue, hand-delivered to your hotel or home if you're in Vaughan or Thornhill. We carry a kit for last-minute thread emergencies.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="feature-num">№ VI</div>
          <h3 class="h-3">Lifetime adjustments</h3>
          <p class="body-prose" style="margin-top: 12px;">Bodies change. So do anniversaries. Bring the suit back any time for a re-press, a small letting-out, or a quiet refresh. The pattern remains in our notebook.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- TESTIMONIALS -->
  <section class="section tight">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
        <div class="chapter-no">No. 05</div>
        <h2 class="h-1" style="text-transform: uppercase; max-width: 18ch;">From the <em>groom's side.</em></h2>
        <div class="right">Letters, after the wedding</div>
      </div>
      <div class="quotes" data-reveal-stagger>
        <blockquote class="quote">
          <span class="quote__mark">“</span>
          <p class="quote__text">Sam made the suit. My wife says I made the speech. The photos make it look like the suit made both.</p>
          <div class="quote__attr">J. Halberstam · Groom, 2025</div>
        </blockquote>
        <blockquote class="quote">
          <span class="quote__mark">“</span>
          <p class="quote__text">Twelve men, one fitting. Every father, brother and best man stood in the same line and looked like they belonged to one family — which is the whole point.</p>
          <div class="quote__attr">E. Stein · Groom &amp; brother of two</div>
        </blockquote>
        <blockquote class="quote">
          <span class="quote__mark">“</span>
          <p class="quote__text">It cost more than my first car. Six years later, the car is gone and the suit still fits. Best decision I made for the wedding.</p>
          <div class="quote__attr">B. Friedman · Toronto</div>
        </blockquote>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BOOKING CTA -->
  <section class="section flush">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="booking-block" data-reveal>
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow-rule" style="color: var(--gold-soft); margin-bottom: 28px;">
            <span style="background: var(--navy-deep);">Wedding consultations · By appointment</span>
          </div>
          <h2 class="h-1">Begin a <em>wedding fitting.</em></h2>
          <p class="lede" style="margin-top: 24px;">
            First consultations are usually 9–12 months before the wedding. Bring a photograph of the bride's gown, the venue, and any suit you've loved — or none of those things, and we'll start from a blank page.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="actions">
          <a href="/book" class="btn is-primary" data-open-booking data-no-transition>Book a Wedding Fitting</a>
          <div class="contact-tag" style="margin-top: 12px;">
            Or call the atelier
            <div class="num">647 · 458 · 0711</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
